1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,015
Woman: Jack, I'm thinking of taking the kids to the seaside on a surfing holiday this summer

2
00:00:07,015 --> 00:00:12,860
and I wanted to ask your advice - as I know you're such an expert.

3
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:14,700
Jack: Well, I don't know about that

4
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:19,241
but yes, I've done a bit of surfing over the years.

5
00:00:19,241 --> 00:00:20,160
I'd thoroughly recommend it

6
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:25,302
I think it's the kind of holiday all the family can enjoy together.

7
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:30,088
The thing about surfing is that it's great for all ages and all abilities.

8
00:00:30,088 --> 00:00:32,640
My youngest started when he was only three!

9
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:37,880
Woman: Wow! But it's quite physically demanding, isn't it

10
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,370
I've heard you need to be pretty fit.

11
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:45,060
Jack: Yes. You'll certainly learn more quickly and won't tire as easily.

12
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,820
Woman: Well - that should be OK for us

13
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:51,700
You've been surfing a few times in Ireland, haven't you?

14
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:57,170
Jack: Yes. There's some great surfing there, which people don't always realise.

15
00:00:57,170 --> 00:01:02,570
Woman: And which locations would you recommend? - there seem to be quite a few.

16
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:06,200
Jack: Yes, there are loads. Last year we went to County Donegal

17
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:09,680
There are several great places to surf there.

18
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:16,010
Woman: What about in County Clare? I read that's also really good for surfing.

19
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:21,178
Jack: Yes, it is. I've been there a few times. Most people go to Lahinch.

20
00:01:21,178 --> 00:01:26,670
My kids love it there. The waves aren't too challenging and the town is very lively.

21
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:29,190
Woman: Are there good hotels there?

22
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:31,600
Jack: Yes - some very nice ones

23
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,066
and there are also a few basic hostels and campsites.

24
00:01:35,066 --> 00:01:39,840
It's great if you need lessons as the surf schools are excellent.

25
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,160
Woman: Sounds good.

26
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:44,540
Jack: Yes and there's lots to see in the area -

27
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,920
like those well-known cliffs -... I've forgotten the name of them...

28
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,820
Woman: Oh don't worry - I can look them up.

29
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:53,895
Jack: I've also been surfing in County Mayo,

30
00:01:53,895 --> 00:01:58,337
which is less well-known for surfing, but we had a really good time.

31
00:01:58,337 --> 00:02:02,095
That was a few years ago when the kids were younger.

32
00:02:02,095 --> 00:02:05,170
There's a good surf school at Carrowniskey beach.

33
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:06,730
Woman: How do you spell that?

34
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:18,640
Jack: C-A-double R-O-W-N-I-S-K-E-Y Woman: OK.

35
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:24,230
Jack: I put the kids into the surf camp they run during the summer for 10-16 year olds.

36
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:27,510
Woman: Oh right. How long was that for?

37
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:29,880
Jack: Three hours every day for a week

38
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:33,870
It was perfect - they were so tired out after that.

39
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:35,220
Woman: I can imagine.

40
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:42,381
Jack: One thing we did while the kids were surfing was to rent some kayaks to have a look around the bay

41
00:02:42,381 --> 00:02:44,660
which is nearby. It's really beautiful.

42
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:48,830
Woman: Oh, I'd love to do that.

43
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:53,840
Woman: Now the only time I went to Ireland it rained practically every day.

44
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:58,730
Jack: Mmm yes - that can be a problem - but you can surf in the rain, you know.

45
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:02,130
Woman: It doesn't have the same appeal, somehow.

46
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:07,479
Jack: Well, the weather's been fine the last couple of years when I've been there,

47
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:12,199
but actually, it tends to rain more in August than in the spring or autumn.

48
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:15,660
September's my favourite month because the water is warmer then.

49
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:19,570
Woman: The only problem is that the kids are back to school then.

50
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:26,712
Jack: I know. But one good thing about Irish summers is that it doesn't get too hot.

51
00:03:26,712 --> 00:03:29,520
The average temperature is about 19 degrees

52
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:33,060
and it usually doesn't go above 25 degrees.

53
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:37,220
Woman: That sounds alright. Now what about costs?

54
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,920
Jack: Surfing is a pretty cheap holiday really

55
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:42,924
the only cost is the hire of equipment.

56
00:03:42,924 --> 00:03:50,055
You can expect to pay a daily rate of about 30 euros for the hire of a wetsuit and board -

57
00:03:50,055 --> 00:03:54,690
but you can save about 40 euros if you hire by the week.

58
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:56,060
Woman: That's not too bad.

59
00:03:56,060 --> 00:04:00,540
Jack: No. It's important to make sure you get good quality wetsuits

60
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,716
you'll all get too cold if you don't.

61
00:04:03,716 --> 00:04:06,000
And make sure you also get boots

62
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:11,040
They keep your feet warm and it's easier to surf with them on too.

63
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:15,000
Woman: OK. Well, thanks very much...
